rrelations would be near zero. They're not. They're modest but meaningful. So while your skepticism is logically sound in theory, the empirical reality is that personality tests do capture something real—something that survives the noise of faking and still predicts how people actually perform. That's why so many organizations, from Fortune 500 companies to government agencies, continue to use them as part of their hiring process.
